# Shell scripts must be LF: a CRLF shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) makes the Linux container's entrypoint fail
# with "env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory". eol=lf forces LF even where core.autocrlf is on (Windows).
# The comfy-nodes/comfy-patches rules below are LAST, so any .sh they vendor stays byte-for-byte, not this.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Patch payloads are compared BYTE FOR BYTE against a ComfyUI install: the app decides whether a patch is
# applied by reverse-applying it and seeing whether the tree matches. An end-of-line conversion on checkout
# would make every file differ on one platform and not the other, so a Windows clone would report patches as
# conflicted that a Linux clone reports as applied. Check these out exactly as they are stored.
comfy-patches/** -text
comfy-nodes/**   -text
